export const title = "Schedule Setting Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Schedule Setting Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<p>For every event action setting, you can specify a schedule that determines when an action should be triggered when an event occurs.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 300\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"120\" width=\"150\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f3f4f7\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"105\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\">Event</text>\n  <line x1=\"180\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"360\" cy=\"150\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"34\" fill=\"#dbe6fb\" stroke=\"#8ea9df\"/>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1b3a7a\">Schedule</text>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"150\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"430\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"220\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"55\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dcefe0\" stroke=\"#7fbf95\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"83\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#20603a\">Action Handler</text>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"127\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dcefe0\" stroke=\"#7fbf95\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#20603a\">Action Handler</text>\n  <rect x=\"540\" y=\"197\" width=\"150\" height=\"46\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#dcefe0\" stroke=\"#7fbf95\"/>\n  <text x=\"615\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#20603a\">Action Handler</text>\n  <line x1=\"360\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"260\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrS)\"/>\n  <text x=\"375\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#5b6270\">drop</text>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrS\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Schedule Overview</h2>\n<p>Schedules are recurring and follow a defined cycle. You can set weekly, monthly, or yearly schedules.</p>\n<p>In addition to regular schedules, you can also configure a schedule as an <strong>Exclusion Schedule</strong>. An exclusion schedule works in reverse of a normal schedule &mdash; it prevents the action from firing during its time range. Exclusion schedules take priority over regular schedules, so if the time an event occurs falls within both a regular schedule and an exclusion schedule, the action will not be triggered.</p>\n<p>Event action schedules operate according to the policy below.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-weight:700;\">&#8251; Schedule Policy</p>\n<ol style=\"margin:0;\">\n<li>If no schedule is set on an event action, every occurring event always triggers the configured action.</li>\n<li>If multiple schedules are registered on an event action, the action fires if any one of those schedules is true.</li>\n<li>If the event falls within an exclusion schedule, the action does not fire, even if another schedule is true.</li>\n<li>Schedules are configured per event action, but once a schedule is created it can be referenced from any event action item.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Creating a New Schedule</h2>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:560px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div style=\"display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:10px;\">\n    <span style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:13px;\">Schedule Setting</span>\n    <span class=\"btn small primary\">Setting</span>\n  </div>\n  <table class=\"app-table\">\n    <tr><th>Name</th><th>Operation</th></tr>\n    <tr><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;color:var(--text-muted);\">-</td></tr>\n  </table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>You can add a schedule from the event action settings screen by clicking the <strong>Setting</strong> button in the Schedule Setting area.</p>\n<p>To create a new schedule, click the <strong>Add New</strong> button at the bottom of the schedule list.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:520px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:150px 1fr;font-size:12.5px;\">\n    <span>Name</span><input placeholder=\"Schedule preset name\" disabled>\n    <span>Schedule Cycle</span><select disabled><option>Weekly</option></select>\n    <span>Schedule Designation</span><select disabled><option>Day-based</option></select>\n    <span>Schedule</span><select disabled><option>Day</option></select>\n    <span>Time Range</span><span style=\"display:flex;gap:6px;align-items:center;\"><input value=\"00:00\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"> ~ <input value=\"00:00\" disabled style=\"width:80px;\"></span>\n    <span>Exclusion Schedule</span><label style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled> Set this as exclusion schedule</label>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Name</strong> &ndash; enter a name to identify the schedule (e.g. Working Hours, Holiday).</li>\n<li><strong>Schedule Cycle</strong> &ndash; sets the schedule's repeat cycle. Can be set to weekly, monthly, or yearly.</li>\n<li><strong>Schedule Designation</strong> &ndash; specifies whether the schedule is day-of-week based or date based.</li>\n<li><strong>Schedule and Time Range</strong> &ndash; set the applicable day(s)/date(s) and the time range.</li>\n<li><strong>Exclusion Schedule</strong> &ndash; checking this sets the schedule as an exclusion schedule.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>Weekly Schedule</h2>\n<p>A weekly schedule can't reference a specific date, so its schedule designation is always fixed to day-of-week based.</p>\n<p>You configure the schedule by selecting the target day(s) of the week and a time range. For example, you could set up a schedule for every Monday through Friday.</p>\n\n<h2>Monthly Schedule</h2>\n<p>When a monthly schedule uses day-of-week based designation, you can specify a week number within the month along with the day(s) of the week. For example: the 2nd Monday&ndash;Friday of every month.</p>\n<p>When a monthly schedule uses date-based designation, you can specify the actual date(s) within the month. For example: the 1st, the 15th, and the last day of every month.</p>\n\n<h2>Yearly Schedule</h2>\n<p>When a yearly schedule uses day-of-week based designation, you can specify the applicable month(s) along with the week number and day(s) of week within each. For example: the 2nd Monday&ndash;Friday of January&ndash;March every year.</p>\n<p>When a yearly schedule uses date-based designation, you can specify the applicable month(s) and date(s) within each. For example: the 1st, 15th, and last day of January&ndash;March every year.</p>\n\n<h2>Time Range Setting</h2>\n<p>The schedule's time range sets the hours during which it is active on its specified day(s). Time ranges follow the policy below.</p>\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--border);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<ol style=\"margin:0;\">\n<li>If the start time is earlier than the end time, the schedule applies to that time range within the day (e.g. 09:00&ndash;18:00).</li>\n<li>If the start time equals the end time, the schedule applies to the full 24 hours of that day (e.g. 00:00&ndash;00:00).</li>\n<li>If the start time is later than the end time, the schedule applies from the start time on that day through to the end time on the following day (e.g. 21:00&ndash;09:00).</li>\n</ol>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Exclusion Schedule</h2>\n<p>Any schedule can be set as an exclusion schedule. Exclusion schedules take priority over regular schedules &mdash; if any exclusion schedule registered on an event action is active, the action will not fire, regardless of any other schedule that is also true.</p>";
